{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And what of the land, whether it is fat</b> — meaning, whether it yields fatness in its fruits. <b>Whether it is lean</b> — meaning, whether, when it puts forth its strength into the fruits, it becomes lean on that account, in the manner of lands that are sown one year and left fallow one year so that they not become exhausted; or whether they are sown year after year and it does not diminish in its strength but produces a second [crop] like the first — for this would indicate that it does not suffer depletion from its cultivation." "<b>Whether there is tree</b> — meaning the name of the species: whether there is in it every species of tree. <b>Whether there is none</b> — meaning whether there is a tree that is not found in it — and this is the verse's statement (Deuteronomy 8:9): ״לֹא תֶחְסַר כֹּל בָּהּ״."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:23.935355376Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}